      "side": 1,
      "message": "This if statement conflicts with the commit message, here we\u0027re checking for ISH disabled so if the ISH is disabled then we disable the lid IMU interrupt and enable the base accel interrupt?\n\nWe should enumerate the code paths here (it\u0027s a little complicated because we\u0027re trying to still support older devices).\n\n1. Running on EC with ISH disabled\nIn this case, the if statement on line 64 will fail so everything should execute as usual. We\u0027ll get the form factor and check for clamshell. If we\u0027re in clamshell we\u0027ll disable the GMR switch, disable the lid imu interrupt, and set the base accel pin.\n\n2. Running on EC with ISH enabled\nIn this case we\u0027ll go into line 65 and disable the sensors. I think what this CL tries to do is also get into line 89 with the call to gmr_tablet_switch_disable() if we\u0027re in clamshell mode.\n\n3. Running on ISH\nIn this case we\u0027ll skip the entire if statement on line 56 and just check for clamshell.\n\n--------------------------------\nSo I think we\u0027re solving for case #2 here in which case I would suggest just moving the call to get the FORM_FACTOR all the way up to the top of the function and just adding the following right before the return on line 77:\n\n```c\nif (sensor_fwconfig \u003d\u003d FORM_FACTOR_CLAMSHELL) {\n  gmr_tablet_switch_disable();\n}\n```",
      "revId": "cf3e4ffebcac8507592b5586df6b02ec5c6591f2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a369c39_b1afee54",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/trulo/uldrenite/src/sensor.c",
